         recommended test: A benchmark scoring or experiment script sets the batch option in the run configuration to on, and the run's Claude calls are then submitted via the Message Batches API rather than called directly.
           inputs:  One RunConfig(batch=True, mode=RECORD, transcript_root=tmp_path) and the `provider` FakeProvider fixture. Call config.build_client() twice to get two clients, then issue many distinct calls concurrently (e.g. 10 questions split across the two clients via map_calls under calls_in_flight(512)).
           detects: `build_client` creates a new MessageBatcher on each call. A script that builds several clients from one config, or calls `build_client` repeatedly, gets separate batchers. Their calls are never gathered into the same batch, which defeats the batch behaviour the setting is meant to give.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion batch-opt-in-switchable-by-scripts

