Ways the change could fail a criterion (what each rating is measured against):

  min-reusable-prefix-512-tokens
    [boundary_wrong_side] min-reusable-prefix-512-tokens/exact-512-opening-not-marked
      The comparison in mark_reusable_opening (not shown in the diff, but it consumes _minimum_reusable_opening) may be strict (> minimum) rather than inclusive. An opening of exactly 512 tokens would then get no cache breakpoint on Sonnet 5.5, Opus 5.5 or Haiku 5.5.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#3
      pairs: 12 put to the model, 271 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] min-reusable-prefix-512-tokens/sonnet-5-5-resolved-as-sonnet-5
      Model-name resolution uses prefix matching against a table in which 'sonnet-5' (1024) and 'sonnet-5-5' (512) both match a Sonnet 5.5 name. If the longest-match rule fails, or the model is spelled in a form that does not start with the 'sonnet-5-5' key (for example 'claude-sonnet-5.5' with a dot), Sonnet 5.5 falls back to the Sonnet 5 minimum of 1024. Openings between 512 and 1023 tokens are then unmarked.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#3
      src/acceptance/llm.py#2
