  [already_present] batch-api-opt-in/batch-gate-uses-explicit-marker-predicate
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 28 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 255 skipped once the defect was covered
    Line 1323 gates batching on `_needs_explicit_marker(request["model"])`, which is true only when the provider prefix is exactly `anthropic`. Any Claude model reached through another route, such as Bedrock or Vertex, is therefore sent directly even in a batched run. That is the DEFECTIVE behaviour. The repair gates on the model being a Claude model instead, so every Claude call is batched.

