  [already_present] batch-opt-in-switchable-by-scripts/batch-gated-on-explicit-marker-and-default-completion
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 4 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 279 skipped once the defect was covered
    Lines 1320-1324 already gate batching on `self._completion_fn is _default_completion_fn` (1322) and `_needs_explicit_marker(request["model"])` (1323). So Claude calls on routes where the marker check is false, or through a non-default completion function, are sent directly even with a batcher present. That is the DEFECTIVE behaviour. The repair replaces both conditions with a model-name check for Claude, so those calls are batched when batch is on. This is a judgment call: the marker check also serves as the Anthropic test, so a name-based test stands in for it.

  [not_mutable] batch-opt-in-switchable-by-scripts/batch-option-not-threaded-through-all-script-entry-points
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 283 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    The defect concerns other benchmark scoring and experiment entry points that build a RunConfig and do not forward batch. All the regions offered are in instability.py. There, run_once builds RunConfig with batch=batch (line 733), and measure_instability forwards batch to both run_once calls (lines 856, 872). Any other RunConfig-building path lives in files I cannot see, so I cannot tell whether it forwards batch. An edit inside the offered regions would only drop batch from the instability path itself, which is not the named defect.

  [already_present] batch-opt-in-switchable-by-scripts/batcher-per-build-client-not-shared
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 283 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    Line 233, `batcher=MessageBatcher() if self.batch else None`, constructs a fresh MessageBatcher on every build_client call, so clients built from one config never share a batch. That is the DEFECTIVE behaviour. The repair caches one batcher on the config instance via `self.__dict__.setdefault`, so every client built from the same config shares it. This assumes RunConfig has a `__dict__` (no slots), which I could not see in the shown code. The EXPECTED sentence's 'at least each go through some batcher' clause also holds today, but the sharing clause does not, so I treated the code as defective.

  [already_present] batch-opt-in-switchable-by-scripts/concurrency-wrapper-breaks-on-defaulted-client
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 12 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 271 skipped once the defect was covered
    Line 405 does `signature.bind(*args, **kwargs).arguments["client"]`. `bind` does not apply parameter defaults, so a call that omits `client` and relies on a default has no `client` entry and raises KeyError. That is the DEFECTIVE behaviour. The repair applies defaults and reads `client` with `.get`, so the wrapper never raises and still passes the client's limit to `calls_in_flight`. I did not address the second half of the defect, that only `run_review` is wrapped. That part would need edits in other places.

