  [already_present] byte-identical-review-state-across-send-modes/identical-requests-share-one-batched-answer
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 12 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 271 skipped once the defect was covered
    Line 167 derives custom_id only from the beta header and body via _custom_id. Lines 169-173 then reuse the same waiting Future for any identical custom_id, so identical concurrent requests become one batch entry and share one answer. That is the DEFECTIVE behaviour. The repair mixes the calling thread's id and a monotonic timestamp into the hashed text, so each call gets its own custom_id and its own batch entry, as in direct sending. The id is still a 64-hex SHA-256 digest, so the batch's custom_id length limit still holds.

